From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:41:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 416/443] [ae-patch] Show the compaction strip only for manual
 compact, not Claude's background auto precompute

Claude Code fires PreCompact with trigger=auto when it starts precomputing a summary in the background at about 85 percent of the auto-compact window, and applies it only when context reaches the window, possibly never. The forwarder treated every PreCompact as a compaction in progress, so the web strip eased to about 97 percent and hung. Parse the trigger from the hook payload; an auto PreCompact now posts no status but still mints the pending token, so the boundary persists once when SessionStart source=compact arrives. Manual /compact keeps the strip.
